From e2cd9d1363b1f3d73b34cfb419777fbda873c7b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Schaefer <stefanschaefer@BlackGuard.fritz.box>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 02:04:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] API keys: new scope "Realtime Data" for live sandworms, NPCs,
 vehicles and storms

Realtime Data is its own read-only namespace (realtime:read), shown as a
separate row "Realtime Data" (None / Read) when creating an API key. The
Console proxies the optional MapViewer3D position agent (mvagent on
127.0.0.1:8796, no login) so every request goes through the normal API key /
session authorization:

- GET /api/realtime/healthz, /api/realtime/objects, /api/realtime/stream (SSE)
- player positions only with players:read as well; otherwise removed from
  snapshots and position updates
- open streams re-check the key every 10 s: disabling, expiring, revoking or
  removing the scope ends the stream; 4 streams per key, 16 in total
- no process ids are passed on; agent URL must be plain HTTP on loopback
- tiers: owner and admin; maps:read does not include it
- tests: test/realtime.test.js, scope/RBAC parity tests, ApiKeysSection test;
  docs/console/realtime.md and the api-keys scope table

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
